node_modules/
# A symlink named node_modules is not a directory, so the pattern above
# misses it. One was committed into packages/verify, pointing at another
# package's install: a link that dangles on a fresh clone.
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dist/

# Foundry build output. lib/ is a submodule and stays tracked; the generated
# Solidity fixture and the recorded gate results do not, because a reader
# should be able to see what the tests asserted without running a build.
packages/contracts/out/
packages/contracts/cache/
packages/contracts/broadcast/
# One forge run, written down so every gate can read it instead of starting
# its own. Temporary by definition: the recorders consume it and delete it.
packages/contracts/gates-run.json
# A local anvil deployment is a throwaway; deployments/ is for chains a reader
# can go and look at.
packages/contracts/deployments/31337.json
# The root lockfile. Each workspace commits its own — those nine are tracked —
# and the root one is whatever `npm install --include-workspace-root` last
# resolved across all of them. It has never been committed, CI regenerates it
# on every run, and an 800-package file nobody reviews is one that only ever
# shows up as noise in a diff. The leading slash keeps the per-package ones.
/package-lock.json
*.log
# The meter's snapshot. A cache by definition: delete it and the meter rebuilds
# it from chain, which is the property its tests assert.
packages/meter/ledger.*.json
packages/attest/ledger.*.json
design/cordon-surfaces.html
.DS_Store
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Bundled fresh from packages/ui on every brand build.
packages/brand/src/dotfont.cjs

# Kept out of the repository deliberately. The plan and the brief are how this
# project is built and what it is betting on, not what it ships, and this
# repository is public. The working rules are the same story in engineering
# terms, so they stay out too — they are how the code got written, not part of
# what it does. The invariants they name are asserted by the tests, which is
# where a reader should be able to find them anyway.
PLAN.md
NEXT.md
CLAUDE.md
# The repository root's own docs folder, not any package's. The site's
# documentation lives in packages/site/src/docs and ships.
/docs/
.claude/
